"
I am the trait shared by the smoke tests that run the class-side methods having a pragma, one test per method. I hold everything they share; `TSmokeScriptMethodsTest` and `TSmokeSampleInstanceMethodsTest` add their pragma and their test.

The design is modular: no class of `SUnit-SmokeVerifier` checks anything. Each package or project gets its own test classes, generated by `ProjectSmokeVerifierGenerator`, which are subclasses of `ParametrizedTestCase` using one of my two traits and defining only which packages they check.

## Responsibility:

- Find the class-side methods with the pragma of the test (`pragmaSelector`) in the packages to check, except the excluded ones, and give one to each test (`testParameters`).
- Run a method on its class (`runMethod`).
- Never pass while checking nothing: `setUp` fails when there is no package to check, when one of them is not loaded (naming it), or when no method has the pragma.

## Collaborators:

- `ParametrizedTestCase` and `ParametrizedTestMatrix`: the class using me sets `method` for each test.
- `TSmokeScriptMethodsTest` and `TSmokeSampleInstanceMethodsTest`: the traits using me.
- `ProjectSmokeVerifierGenerator`: generates the classes using those traits.
- `Package`: answers the methods of a package, extensions included.

## Public API and Key Messages

- Class side, required: `packageNamesToCheck` and `pragmaSelector`. Class side, to override: `excludedMethods`, strings such as `'MyClass class>>#resetAll'`.
- A project does not use me directly:

```
ProjectSmokeVerifierGenerator new
	projectName: 'MyProject';
	packageNames: #( 'MyProject-Core' 'MyProject-UI' );
	testPackageName: 'MyProject-Tests';
	generate
```

## Internal Representation

- `method`: the class-side method checked by a test, set by the test matrix.

### Implementation Points

- `testParameters` answers an empty matrix when there is no method: `ParametrizedTestCase>>#setUp` cannot use a matrix without options. The single test is then run without method and fails in `setUp`.
- I know nothing about user interfaces: the windows a method opens stay open. A project that wants to close them overrides `runMethod` in its generated class, in its own package. A method opening a modal dialog blocks the test: exclude it.
"
Trait {
	#name : 'TSmokePragmaMethodsTest',
	#instVars : [
		'method'
	],
	#category : 'SUnit-SmokeVerifier',
	#package : 'SUnit-SmokeVerifier'
}

{ #category : 'accessing' }
TSmokePragmaMethodsTest classSide >> excludedMethods [
	"Answer the methods I do not run, as strings such as 'MyClass class>>#resetAll'. Override it in a copy to exclude methods that must not be run by a test."

	^ #(  )
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
TSmokePragmaMethodsTest classSide >> methodsToCheck [
	"Answer the class-side methods with my pragma in the packages to check, except the excluded ones."

	| packages |
	packages := (self packageNamesToCheck collect: [ :each | self packageOrganizer packageNamed: each ifAbsent: [ nil ] ]) reject: [ :each | each isNil ].
	^ ((packages flatCollect: [ :package |
		package methods select: [ :each | each methodClass isClassSide and: [ each hasPragmaNamed: self pragmaSelector ] ] ])
		reject: [ :each | self excludedMethods includes: each printString ]) asArray
		sort: [ :a :b | a printString <= b printString ]
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
TSmokePragmaMethodsTest classSide >> missingPackageNames [
	"Answer the names of the packages to check that are not loaded."

	^ self packageNamesToCheck reject: [ :each | self packageOrganizer hasPackage: each ]
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
TSmokePragmaMethodsTest classSide >> packageNamesToCheck [
	"Answer the names of the packages whose methods I check. The class generated for a project by ProjectSmokeVerifierGenerator answers the packages of the project."

	^ self explicitRequirement
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
TSmokePragmaMethodsTest classSide >> pragmaSelector [
	"Answer the pragma of the class-side methods I check."

	^ self explicitRequirement
]

{ #category : 'building suites' }
TSmokePragmaMethodsTest classSide >> testParameters [
	"Answer one option per method to check, or an empty matrix when there is none: ParametrizedTestCase>>#setUp cannot use a matrix without options."

	| methods |
	methods := self methodsToCheck.
	methods ifEmpty: [ ^ ParametrizedTestMatrix new ].
	^ ParametrizedTestMatrix new
		forSelector: #method addOptions: methods;
		yourself
]

{ #category : 'running' }
TSmokePragmaMethodsTest >> assertPackagesToCheckAreLoaded [
	"Fail when there is no package to check or when one of them is not loaded: a test checking nothing must not pass."

	| missing |
	self deny: self class packageNamesToCheck isEmpty description: 'No package to check'.
	missing := self class missingPackageNames.
	missing ifNotEmpty: [ self fail: ('Packages to check not loaded: {1}' format: { ', ' join: missing }) ]
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
TSmokePragmaMethodsTest >> method [

	^ method
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
TSmokePragmaMethodsTest >> method: aCompiledMethod [

	method := aCompiledMethod
]

{ #category : 'running' }
TSmokePragmaMethodsTest >> runMethod [
	"Answer the result of running my method on its class. A class using me can override it, for example to close the windows the method opens."

	^ method valueWithReceiver: method methodClass instanceSide
]

{ #category : 'running' }
TSmokePragmaMethodsTest >> setUp [

	super setUp.
	self assertPackagesToCheckAreLoaded.
	method ifNil: [ self fail: ('No class-side method with <{1}> in the packages to check' format: { self class pragmaSelector }) ]
]
